ile the cottages have now, so nothing changes from the road. The fastener count does not change either.</p></li><li class="shared"><span class="num">0 7</span><span class="tag shared">Same in every option</span><h3>Permit fees, dump fees, workers&rsquo; compensation, general liability and sales tax are inside the price.</h3><p>None of it comes back later as an extra. Some estimates leave the tax line for the final invoice; this one does not.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#10003;</span><h3>Warranty</h3><p>Manufacturer coverage follows the finish: AZ-50 substrate with a premium paint finish carries 50/30 year terms, standard paint 40/30 year, and AZ-55 unpainted mill finish 25 year. No coastal rust warranty applies to this product at this address.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#43;</span><h3>Included in the price</h3><p>All installation conforms to state and local building codes.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#43;</span><h3>Included in the price</h3><p>Cleaning and disposal of all roofing debris from rooftop and grounds.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#43;</span><h3>Included in the price</h3><p>Permit fees, dump fees, workers&rsquo; compensation, general liability and taxes included in the price.</p></li></ol>
    <p class="body rv d3">Replacing an exposed-fastener roof with another exposed-fastener roof reproduces the condition described in the inspection. That is a defensible choice on budget grounds. It is not a fix for the cause.</p>
  </div>
</section><section id="product-7">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rail rv"><span>0 7 &middot; Option B</span><span class="mid">&middot;</span><span class="t2">Concealed fastener steel</span></div>
    <h1 class="h1 rv d1">Better steel, no exposed screws.</h1>
    <p class="sub rv d1">The upgrade that removes the fastener problem without changing material.</p>
    <div class="cols"><div><p class="body rv d2">CoastalMAX&reg; is a steel panel coated with a zinc, aluminium and magnesium alloy rather than zinc alone. Premier Metal Roofing builds it for coastal work and finishes it in Kynar 500&reg; PVDF colours. Their PermaShield100&trade; is a 16&Prime; standing seam profile.</p><p class="body rv d2">The panels clip to the deck underneath the metal. On the field of the roof there is no screw through the panel face at all, which removes the thousands of small sealed holes that started the problem on your current roofs.</p><p class="body rv d2">There is a limit, and it is the reason this option is not the recommendation. Read the warranty note below before you weigh the price against Option C.</p><figure class="shot rv d2"><img src="https://arrysroofing.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Giebner2.jpg" alt="A concealed-fastener standing seam metal roof installed by Arry&rsquo;s Roofing, with no exposed fasteners across the panel faces" loading="lazy"><figcaption>OUR OWN WORK &middot; CONCEALED FASTENER STANDING SEAM</figcaption></figure></div><div class="panel rv d2"><div class="eyebrow">CoastalMAX&reg; concealed fastener</div><dl class="dl"><div><dt>Panel material</dt><dd>Steel with a zinc-aluminium-magnesium alloy coating</dd></div><div><dt>Fastening</dt><dd class="hi">Concealed &mdash; no screws through the panel face on the field</dd></div><div><dt>Profile</dt><dd>PermaShield100&trade;, 16&Prime; standing seam</dd></div><div><dt>Finish</dt><dd>Kynar 500&reg; PVDF resin, fade-resistive colours</dd></div><div><dt>Corrosion resistance</dt><dd>Substantially better than standard galvanized steel</dd></div><div><dt>Published coastal warranty</dt><dd>25-year coastal corrosion warranty on PermaShield&trade; systems</dd></div><div><dt>Coastal approval</dt><dd>Zero-foot setback from Marco Island to the Big Bend, and non-breaking-surf intracoastals; 300 ft setback required from breaking surf</dd></div><div><dt>Coastal rust warranty at this address</dt><dd class="hi">Not offered &mdash; the property sits inside the breaking-surf setback</dd></div><div><dt>Replaces</dt><dd>The existing 5V-Crimp galvanized steel roofs</dd></div></dl><div class="note">Product and setback data read from the manufacturer&rsquo;s published CoastalMAX&reg; and PermaShield&trade; material, August 2026. Panel gauge, colour and final profile would be confirmed on the contract.</div></div></div>
    
    <div class="statblock rv d2"><div class="sb"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">Exposed fasteners on the field</div></div><div class="sb"><div class="n">16<small>&Prime;</small></div><div class="l">Standing seam panel width</div></div><div class="sb"><div class="n">3</div><div class="l">Metals in the coating: zinc, aluminium, magnesium</div></div><div class="sb"><div class="n">300<small>ft</small></div><div class="l">Setback the coastal warranty needs</div></div></div>
    
    
    <p class="body rv d3">Judge this option on one question. Is losing the exposed fasteners enough on its own? On the bayside buildings the honest answer is probably yes. On the six cottages in the front row, facing breaking surf, the manufacturer has already given you their answer.</p>
  </div>
</section><section id="scope-8" class="dark">
