    <p class="body rv d3">This system performs markedly better than the galvanized steel it replaces. I am telling you plainly that it still arrives without coastal rust coverage here, because the setback rule is written about beachfront addresses like this one.</p>
  </div>
</section><section id="product-9">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rail rv"><span>0 9 &middot; Option C</span><span class="mid">&middot;</span><span class="t2">Marine-grade aluminium</span></div>
    <h1 class="h1 rv d1">The metal salt cannot rust.</h1>
    <p class="sub rv d1">The only one of the three that comes with a coastal rust warranty at this address.</p>
    <div class="cols"><div><p class="body rv d2">This system uses heavy-gauge 0.032&Prime; marine-grade aluminium panels, installed with a concealed fastener system on stainless steel clips and stainless accessories. Aluminium does not rust. That is a property of the metal, not of a coating applied to it.</p><p class="body rv d2">Everything else on this property has been a coating protecting steel: zinc on the panels you have now, an alloy on Option B. Once the coating goes, the steel underneath is exposed. There is no equivalent moment here.</p><p class="body rv d2">It carries a 25-year manufacturer coastal rust warranty for this property. Options A and B do not, and the setback rules that exclude them are written about beachfront addresses like yours.</p><figure class="shot rv d2"><img src="https://arrysroofing.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Sanchez1.jpg" alt="A concealed-fastener metal roof installed by Arry&rsquo;s Roofing on a coastal property" loading="lazy"><figcaption>OUR OWN WORK &middot; CONCEALED FASTENER METAL ON THE COAST</figcaption></figure></div><div class="panel rv d2"><div class="eyebrow">0.032&Prime; marine-grade aluminium</div><dl class="dl"><div><dt>Panel material</dt><dd>0.032&Prime; heavy-gauge marine-grade aluminium</dd></div><div><dt>Fastening</dt><dd>Concealed, on stainless steel clips</dd></div><div><dt>Accessories</dt><dd>Stainless steel throughout</dd></div><div><dt>Corrosion behaviour</dt><dd>Aluminium does not rust in a salt environment</dd></div><div><dt>Coastal rust warranty</dt><dd class="hi">25-year manufacturer coastal rust warranty for this property</dd></div><div><dt>Setback requirement</dt><dd class="hi">None &mdash; approved at this beachfront address</dd></div><div><dt>Replaces</dt><dd>The existing 5V-Crimp galvanized steel roofs</dd></div></dl><div class="note">Warranty term as stated in the 15 July inspection summary. Panel profile, colour, finish and the manufacturer&rsquo;s registration would be confirmed on the contract.</div></div></div>
    
    <div class="statblock rv d2"><div class="sb"><div class="n">25<small>yr</small></div><div class="l">Coastal rust warranty here</div></div><div class="sb"><div class="n">0.032<small>&Prime;</small></div><div class="l">Panel thickness</div></div><div class="sb"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">Exposed fasteners on the field</div></div><div class="sb"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">Ferrous metal in the assembly</div></div></div>
    
    
    <p class="body rv d3">This is the highest number on the page and the lowest risk on the property. On six buildings in the front row facing open Gulf, it is the option I would put on my own rental units.</p>
  </div>
