    <ol class="cardstack rv d2"><li class="shared"><span class="num">0 1</span><span class="tag shared">Same in every option</span><h3>Remove the existing 5V-Crimp exposed-fastener galvanized panels, perimeter trim and fasteners from all six Gulf-side buildings, down to the deck.</h3><p>Nothing new goes over the top of a corroded roof. Everything comes off so the decking underneath can actually be looked at.</p></li><li class="shared"><span class="num">0 2</span><span class="tag shared">Same in every option</span><h3>Replace soft and deteriorated wood along the eaves, and deteriorated roof decking, including the areas identified at Beachside Cottage #2.</h3><p>Rotted framing has nothing solid left to hold a fastener. This is the work that has to happen before any panel system can be fixed down over it.</p></li><li class="shared"><span class="num">0 3</span><span class="tag shared">Same in every option</span><h3>Rebuild the missing front and rear fascia boards at Beachside Cottage #2.</h3><p>With the fascia gone, the roof edge has been open to wind-driven rain and salt spray. It gets closed as part of the roof, not as a call-back afterwards.</p></li><li class="shared"><span class="num">0 4</span><span class="tag shared">Same in every option</span><h3>Replace all pipe boots, vent flashings, vent collars and penetration flashings.</h3><p>Penetrations leak before panels do. Replacing them with the roof means the whole assembly is the same age from that day on.</p></li><li class="shared"><span class="num">0 5</span><span class="tag shared">Same in every option</span><h3>New eave trim, rake trim and perimeter metal to match the panel system.</h3><p>The perimeter metal and the clips are aluminium and stainless like the rest of the assembly, so there is no dissimilar metal sitting in salt spray at the edge.</p></li><li class="only"><span class="num">0 6</span><span class="tag only">Only in this option</span><h3>Install 0.032&Prime; marine-grade aluminium panels in a concealed-fastener profile, on stainless steel clips and stainless accessories.</h3><p>Aluminium and stainless are the two metals on this page that salt does not rust. Nothing on the roof is relying on a coating to survive the exposure.</p></li><li class="only"><span class="num">0 7</span><span class="tag only">Only in this option</span><h3>Register the manufacturer&rsquo;s 25-year coastal rust warranty for the property on completion.</h3><p>The warranty only exists once it is registered against this address. It is our job, not yours, and it is inside this price.</p></li><li class="shared"><span class="num">0 8</span><span class="tag shared">Same in every option</span><h3>Permit fees, dump fees, workers&rsquo; compensation, general liability and sales tax are inside the price.</h3><p>None of it comes back later as an extra. Some estimates leave the tax line for the final invoice; this one does not.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#10003;</span><h3>Warranty</h3><p>25-year manufacturer coastal rust warranty for this property, with no setback requirement. This is the only one of the three options that carries coastal rust coverage at this address.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#43;</span><h3>Included in the price</h3><p>All installation conforms to state and local building codes.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#43;</span><h3>Included in the price</h3><p>Cleaning and disposal of all roofing debris from rooftop and grounds.</p></li><li><span class="num">&#43;</span><h3>Included in the price</h3><p>Permit fees, dump fees, workers&rsquo; compensation, general liability and taxes included in the price.</p></li></ol>
    
